sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Go sender
    participant A as SPIRE Agent
    participant S as SPIRE Server
    participant M as Go Money receiver

    A->>S: Bootstrap and node attestation
    S-->>A: Agent identity and authorized registrations
    A->>S: Request or rotate workload certificates
    S-->>A: Signed SVIDs cached by Agent
    C->>A: Fetch X.509-SVID over local Unix socket
    A->>A: Kernel peer PID and UID<br/>Executable SHA-256 and Docker selectors
    A->>A: Every required selector matches
    A-->>C: /caller/trusted SVID, key, trust bundle
    C->>C: Check received ID is /caller/trusted
    C->>M: Begin mutual TLS handshake
    M-->>C: Present server /money SVID
    C->>C: Verify server chain and exact /money ID
    C->>M: Present own /caller/trusted SVID<br/>Prove possession of private key
    M->>M: Verify client SVID and trust domain
    C->>M: POST /transfer<br/>Fixed JSON payload and stable request ID
    M->>M: Extract ID from verified TLS state<br/>Authorize exact ID, method, route
    M->>M: Validate bounded JSON and credential expiry
    M->>M: Apply atomic, idempotent ledger transfer
    M-->>C: HTTP 200 and transfer result
